<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One column of verse, full width, with paragraph indents. Page number top left. Running head top centre. Catchword bottom right.</layout>
  <page_number>50</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Vidit</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Extarent hominum luce fruentium,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Omnes unius hipectore Guisii</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Spirabant furiis matribus edita,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Plectenda foret ut perdita Gallia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Fax, quæ dum placido fouit eum sinu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Externum, nimium triftia retulit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Eheu hospitij præmia candidi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Natos namque tuos, Gallia, compulit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Durus dulce solum linquere patrium:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Urbes cæde, domos ignibus, arvaque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Luctu tristifico non semel obruens:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Et legem statuens legibus irritis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Nil non arbitrio figere proprio,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Quo Gallos premeret Bætica sub iuga,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Et regi fieret rex dominans suo:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Romanaq; lupa captus amoribus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Ludebat simulans callidus artifex</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Mentes simplicium: Nursius ut vafer</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Bellacis Marii miles, Ibericos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Olim per populos numina mentiens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Dianæ specie quadrupedis vaga.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Christi membra sequens &amp; varie</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>secans, Fecit, barbaries ut fera Cæsarum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Sit laudata, velut summa benignitas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Testis Parrhisiæ nox truculentiæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Heroum caluit frigida quæ nece.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Nox signata pio sanguine: quem Deus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Fumantem aspiciens luminibus pijs,</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The page number may be 50 or 59; the last digit is a worn old-style figure. Long s is transcribed as s throughout. Some words are uncertain: "hipectore" (the ct ligature is read as ct), "Bætica" (ligature assumed), "Parrhisiæ" and "truculentiæ" (ligatures read as æ). Faint show-through of the facing page appears in the right margin and is not transcribed.</notes>
</page>
